Blender Neural Composer

Historical work: Caffe-GUI-Tool by H. Tomkins, extended by Aaron Wetzler and
Rom Hershkovitz for neural differential operators and Patch-Beltrami research.
Public source: https://github.com/twerdster/caffe-gui-tool
Upstream: https://github.com/hctomkins/caffe-gui-tool
Public source revision consulted: 2de937d9119d6d5ca467fa184c51fc56c5f8f400

neural_operator_blender/caffe_nodes.py and caffe_export.py are modernized
adaptations of the historical project. Historical graph examples and fixed
operator coefficient files in neural_operator_blender/examples/ retain the
original public-domain dedication (Unlicense), reproduced in LICENSES/Unlicense.txt.
Four fixed derivative coefficient files absent from the recovered working tree
(Dmx, Dmy, Dpx, Dpy.prototxt) were recovered from the public revision above.
The six original graph filenames, SHA-256 checksums and recovered node/link
counts are recorded in docs/recovery.json. Only sanitized graph data is
redistributed; original thesis manuscripts and private backup metadata are
not part of this repository.

New interface, interchange, tests, packaging and documentation are available
under the MIT license in LICENSE. The compact untrained operator_demo.json
is also MIT licensed. Blender is a separate application and is not bundled.

This repository incorporates Blender Neural Composer version 1.0.0, revision
76154fe73e305cc6831b296dd071cdcd46fc867d, from
https://github.com/twerdster/blender-neural-composer . Its modern interface,
interchange, tests and tooling retain the MIT license in LICENSES/MIT.txt.
The adaptation of the original Caffe code and recovered coefficient/graph
assets retains the Unlicense, as above. Subsequent modern validation,
compatibility, packaging and optional CPU runtime tooling is also MIT licensed.
The root LICENSE remains the original Unlicense dedication.

The unmodified historical research Caffe schema under tests/schema/ is from
https://github.com/twerdster/caffe , revision
a6083b3ab99a85fc3bf55a9ff84251861d7c6b63. Its third-party BSD license is retained
in LICENSES/Caffe-BSD.txt. It is used only for export validation and is not
bundled in the installable Blender ZIP.
